{{also|Appendix:Variations of "har"}}
==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hæːr/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|sv-här.ogg|Audio|lang=sv}}
* {{rhymes|æːr|lang=sv}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{m|non|hér}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{m|gem-pro|*hē₂r}}.

====Adverb====
{{head|sv|adverb}}

# [[here]]; at this time ''or'' at this place
#: '''''Här''' är den.''
#:: Here it is.

=====Usage notes=====
* In several compounds (''[[härkomst]], [[härledning]], ...''), it is also used like the German adverb {{m|de|her||here, to this place}}, which would translate to Swedish {{m|sv|hit||here, to this place}}, rather than ''här''.

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|sv|där}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|sv|dit}}
* {{l|sv|hädan}}
* {{l|sv|hän}}
* {{l|sv|hit}}

===Etymology 2===
{{PIE root|sv|ker}}
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{m|non|herr}}, from {{etyl|gmq-pro|sv}} {{m|gmq-pro|ᚺᚨᚱᛃᚨ}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{m|gem-pro|*harjaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sv}} {{m|ine-pro|*ker-}}.

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|c}}

# {{label|sv|historical}} a land [[army]]
#: '''''Härarna''' drabbade samman tidigt på morgonen.''
#:: The armies [[clash]]ed in the early morning.

